  "asr_text": "Not what's different between me and that person who earns a lot, but how are my former self and my later self different? In a way, the researchers shifted from comparing yourself with others to keeping track of yourself over time. It's like putting down your binoculars for looking at your neighbor's greener grass and turning the pages of your own records. Then came diligence. Think of it as a personality that takes things seriously and works hard. There was a small positive link between changes in a person's income and later changes in their diligence. In the other direction, there was also a small positive link between changes in diligence and later changes in income. It wasn't a one-way link, but a two-way one. But this is important, so let me stress it. The links were small. So earning more turns me into a more serious person? Hold on before jumping to that conclusion.",
